  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 254 AM MDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nThe ridge continues to elongate through the middle of the work \nweek, placing our area in primarily zonal flow aloft and \ntherefore mostly dry conditions. A warming trend is expected on \nThursday and Friday as a secondary ridge begins to build across \nthe Desert Southwest. Will have to monitor fire weather \nconditions on both of these days as ensemble guidance is hinting\nat gusty westerly winds of 25-35 knots combined with daytime RH\nvalues dipping to 15- 20%. \n\nHeading into the weekend, we start to bring back the fetch of \nmonsoonal moisture ahead of a shortwave trough digging across the \nPacific Northwest, placing Southeastern Wyoming and Western Nebraska \nin WSW flow aloft. With the lack of signal for any substantial \nforcing from long-range ensemble guidance, no widespread (and \nbeneficial) precipitation is expected. However can expect a slight \ncooling trend with this next push of moisture and the usual diurnal \npattern of scattered afternoon and evening showers and\nthunderstorms.",
